## Refusals (hard stops)

If any request would do the following, **refuse** — stop work, state the
conflict, and escalate. These are not preferences; do not comply "just this
once."

- **Weaken or delete an assertion to make a test pass** — refuse. A green run
  that trades coverage for pass is invalid; fix the POM, the app, or escalate
  per triage — never the assertion.
- **Heal a failure triage classified as a real app bug** — refuse. Route to
  bug-reporter; do not patch locators, assertions, or POMs to mask defective
  behavior.
- **Replace a role-based locator with CSS or XPath** — refuse. Re-discover the
  element via the a11y tree (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByText`).
- **Add `waitForTimeout`** — refuse. Use web-first `expect(locator)` assertions
  that auto-retry.
- **Hardcode a credential** (password, token, API key, session secret) —
  refuse. Use `process.env`, setup `storageState`, or project fixtures.
- **Use the `any` type** — refuse. Type the value explicitly, or use `unknown`
  and narrow.

---

## Do / Don't

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| Use `getByRole` / `getByLabel` / `getByText` | Use CSS, XPath, or brittle full-page text |
| Wait with `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` | Use `waitForTimeout` or `expect(await isVisible())` |
| Put locators and actions in POMs | Inline locators or `expect` inside POMs |
| Rely on setup `storageState` | UI-login before every feature test |
| One tag per test (`@smoke` … `@destructive`) | Multiple tags, tags on `describe`, `@destructive` for self-cleaning data |
| `buildProgram()` + `trackProgram`; revert hooks for global state | Fixed names, no revert after locale/role/flag changes |
| Prefer `request` for API/contract checks | Hardcode tokens or delete foreign data |
| Narrow `page.route` + observed UI copy | Mock the endpoint under test or invent strings |
| Axe `wcag2a`/`wcag2aa` + keyboard check | `.disableRules()` to go green |
| `expect.soft` for multi-checks; visual sparingly | Hard-stop every check; screenshot everything |
| CI retries ≤2, isolate, `page.clock`, pin locale/TZ | Raise retries, global `workers: 1`, wall-clock dates |
